We call on the UK Government to uphold its parliamentary commitments and remedy broken promises by:

an immediate moratorium (pause) on disability cuts;

reversing cuts to UC Health & Motability;

launching a review, democratically & independently led by Disabled people and our organisations, including our trade unions.

We call on the House of Commons to reject any further welfare cuts until this remedy is in place, purely on the principle that a promise made in parliament must mean something.
